# Auto-sync conflict avoidance for high-churn shared state (T-SYNC-07).
# active-checkouts.json: two machines bump fenceCounter/updatedAt every ~5 min; a plain
# 3-way merge conflicts every tick and the daemon diverges. Resolve by fenceCounter via
# a custom driver (scripts/merge-lease-state.sh, registered by openclaw-git-sync.sh).
docs/process/state/active-checkouts.json merge=leasestate
# Rendered Tier-1 projections (T-SYNC-15, #986 follow-up): task-queue.md, OPEN_TASKS.md,
# live-status.md, projects.md are 100% DERIVED from tasks.json/projects.json by
# render-tier1-state.py — never hand-edited. Both machines render divergent copies from
# their own pre-merge state, so a plain 3-way merge CONFLICTS on every cross-machine pull.
# With no driver they fell through to the AI-merge fallback, whose smith dispatch timed out
# (240s) and ABORTED the merge every tick — that is what wedged <<MACHINE_2_ID>> (34-behind/13-ahead,
# its real commits stranded off main for days). A union merge is WRONG here (it doubles the
# rendered sections into a corrupt board). Resolve keep-ours (the `true` idiom — no conflict,
# deterministic); openclaw-git-sync.sh then RE-RENDERS these from the merged tasks.json right
# after the pull, so the pushed projection is consistent with merged state before the
# always-on render-consistency pre-push gate. keepours registered by openclaw-git-sync.sh.
docs/process/task-queue.md merge=keepours
docs/process/live-status.md merge=keepours
docs/process/projects.md merge=keepours
workspace/state/OPEN_TASKS.md merge=keepours
# Project live-status is generated from active-checkouts/tasks/file-claims; keep local
# render on merge and regenerate after merged canonical state converges. NOT a render-tier1
# projection (that's live-status.md above) — presence-derived, refreshed out of the drift gate.
docs/process/state/project-live-status.json merge=keepours
docs/process/project-live-status.md merge=keepours
# DOC-INDEX.yaml is generated by build-doc-index.py (NOT tasks.json). Cross-session regens
# conflict on it and the large file times out the Tier-3 AI-merge resolver (240s x3) -> a
# fleet-wide git-sync wedge that stranded <<MACHINE_1_ID>> ahead=12/behind=21 on 2026-08-25. keepours
# keeps each machine's own index; it is regenerated on the next build-doc-index.py / create-gate.
docs/DOC-INDEX.yaml merge=keepours
# session-brief-latest.md is the same class and was the ONE file blocking the fleet on
# 2026-08-17: <<MACHINE_1_ID>> sat ahead=23/behind=27 with the safe auto-heal escalating every 10
# minutes for over an hour, on this file alone, stranding 23 real commits. start-brief.py
# overwrites the whole 33-line snapshot at each session start, so every machine carries its
# own version and a cross-machine convergence conflicts on it EVERY time. It is derived and
# regenerated on the next session start, so keep-ours loses nothing.
workspace/state/session-brief-latest.md merge=keepours
# Daily memory logs (workspace/memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md): append-only reflections written from every
# session on every machine, so a cross-machine convergence 3-way-conflicts on the appended region
# EVERY time (merge:unspecified). That conflict repeatedly wedged the git-sync daemon (2026-08-18:
# it aborted the merge each tick and guard-2 dropped/pinned local commits). union keeps BOTH sides'
# appends — lossless (this is AUTHORED content, so keepours would lose a session's reflections,
# unlike the derived projections above). Verified: union resolves a two-session append conflict
# cleanly with no header duplication. Pattern matches YYYY-MM-DD.md only (not working-context.md,
# personal-log.md, which start with letters and keep their own drivers).
workspace/memory/2???-??-??.md merge=union
